nt) trumps APP** here: the mass increase buys a codebase where `nextGeneration` reads as a named, top-to-bottom sequence (`collectCandidates` → `countLiveNeighbors` → `willBeAlive`) with no manual string decoding, which is a meaningful clarity and correctness-safety win (eliminating the decode step also removes a latent class of bugs if the key format ever changed).\n\n**Tests**: All 10 tests still pass; `tsc --noEmit` is clean.\n\n---\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Renamed `key`→`cellKey`, `live`→`liveCells`, `result`→`nextGenerationCells`; replaced the neighbor-offset IIFE with a static literal table; extracted `willBeAlive` to name the survive/reproduce decision; extracted `collectCandidates` and switched candidate storage from `Set<string>` (with string-parsing decode) to `Map<string, Cell>` to eliminate duplicated coordinate encoding/decoding.\n**Mass Change**: 55 -> 68 (+13, accepted per Rule 2 — clarity over raw mass)\n**Tests**: All 10 passing, `tsc --noEmit` clean"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":1037,"output":2110,"cacheRead":17797,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":20944,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784961367575,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-62dcb333-aea5-4f45-82ee-3320c0c82a5f","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":34580,"output":13398,"cacheRead":133707,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":20944,"turns":11},"model":"requesty/vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","stopReason":"stop"}]}},"isError":false}
