 with an extra named function and a `Map`, and the ternary was extracted into its own function with its own parameter bindings. Per the guidelines, **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) trumps APP** here: the mass increase buys a codebase where `nextGeneration` reads as a named, top-to-bottom sequence (`collectCandidates` → `countLiveNeighbors` → `willBeAlive`) with no manual string decoding, which is a meaningful clarity and correctness-safety win (eliminating the decode step also removes a latent class of bugs if the key format ever changed).\n\n**Tests**: All 10 tests still pass; `tsc --noEmit` is clean.\n\n---\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Renamed `key`→`cellKey`, `live`→`liveCells`, `result`→`nextGenerationCells`; replaced the neighbor-offset IIFE with a static literal table; extracted `willBeAlive` to name the survive/reproduce decision; extracted `collectCandidates` and switched candidate storage from `Set<string>` (with string-parsing decode) to `Map<string, Cell>` to eliminate duplicated coordinate encoding/decoding.\n**Mass Change**: 55 -> 68 (+13, accepted per Rule 2 — clarity over raw mass)\n**Tests**: All 10 passing, `tsc --noEmit` clean"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_06-24-01_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_sonnet-5/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/game-of-life.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/game-of-life.ts\nPassing tests: 10 (all tests in the test list are now implemented and green)\nRecent changes: Added tests for single-cell death, block still-life, blinker oscillation (both transitions), and negative-coordinate handling. All of these passed without implementation changes because the existing survive/reproduce/candidate-set algorithm already generalizes correctly.\n\nThis is the final refactor pass for the whole feature (Conway's Game of Life next-generation function). Do a full 