eighborsOf` helper backed by a precomputed `NEIGHBOR_OFFSETS` constant.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest elements)**: Removed the now-redundant `neighborKeys` function entirely; `nextGeneration` calls `neighborsOf` directly.\n- Naming: no changes needed — existing names already reveal intent.\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Refactoring**: Extracted duplicated neighbor-offset enumeration logic into a single `neighborsOf` helper (backed by a precomputed `NEIGHBOR_OFFSETS` constant), eliminating the redundant `neighborKeys` function.\n**Mass Change**: ~50 → ~17 for the duplicated-logic region (one-time setup cost for the offsets table, reused per call instead of recomputed)\n**Tests**: All 5 passing tests remain green (5 passed, 5 todo)"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_06-24-01_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_sonnet-5/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/game-of-life.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/game-of-life.ts\nPassing tests: 5\nRecent Green phase: Generalized nextGeneration to consider all \"candidate\" cells (currently-live cells plus all of their neighbors), not just live cells. Added a `reproduces(count)` predicate (count === 3) alongside the existing `survives(count)` predicate (count === 2 || count === 3). For each candidate cell, look up whether it's currently alive and apply survives or reproduces accordingly. This makes the full Game of Life ruleset (underpopulation, survival, overpopulation, reproduction) work correctly.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/game-of-life.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/game-of-life.ts\nPassing tests: 5\nRecent Green phase: Generalized nextGeneration to consider all \"candidate\" cells (currently-live cells plus all